/Title (Choosing an engineering branch is oneof the most important academic decisions a student makes, and it shapes later career options. The choice is usually influenced by several factors at once: favourite subjects, technical skills, hobbies, career goals, family advice, salary expectations and industry demand. When educators and academic advisors understand which preferences are common and how they relate to each other, they can plan better counselling, orientation and mentoring activities.)
